fact WorkItem(id: "WI-160", description: some(value: "anthill-todo CLI: track build version. Add a `version` subcommand printing semver + git SHA + build date, and a `--version` flag accepted at any subcommand position. Bake the metadata at build time via build.rs (env var ANTHILL_TODO_VERSION = workspace Cargo version; ANTHILL_TODO_SHA = `git rev-parse --short HEAD`; ANTHILL_TODO_BUILD = ISO-8601 UTC). Surface the same string in `--help` footer. Motivation: today there is no way to tell which build of `anthill-todo` is on PATH; a stale `~/.cargo/bin/anthill-todo` (pre-WI-085 grammar fix) emitted spurious parse warnings against the on-disk workitems file and the diagnosis required diffing binary mtimes. Generalises beyond anthill-todo: every CLI built from this workspace (`anthill`, `anthill-todo`, future tools) should embed the same version stamp, ideally via a small shared crate. Acceptance: cargo test green; `anthill-todo --version` prints a non-empty string; `anthill-todo version` matches; CI/regression test asserts the embedded SHA matches `git rev-parse --short HEAD` at build time."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-06-18T11:19:36Z"))
